      "math_academy_id": "e-12732",
      "problem": "The shaded region below represents the truth set of a predicate $P(x),$ defined over the universal set $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Determine the region that represents the truth set of $\\neg P(x).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130746/assets/cc80d49abe6293acb1325035799dac833a9bcb8f485ed1f785f78c4e1f39b8be.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The truth set of $\\neg P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x){:}$\n\n$$\nT_{\\neg P} = \\overline{T}_P\n$$\n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $\\neg P(x),$ we take all the points that belong to $U$ and do not lie in $T_p,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14130746/assets/86205c3b03c01581677b4fa877dae8c4ca743fe0ac0f1673ef504d548e8c785d.png)",
